<div id="recipe-82992-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82992-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82992"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82992-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">On a large cutting board, finely chop onion and garlic. Sprinkle with kosher salt and knead gently to soften. Transfer to a large bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person chopping onions for ezme." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ezme-sauce.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82992-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Remove the seeds of your tomatoes and give them a fine chop. Alternatively, you can chop them first and strain through a fine mesh strainer to remove the juices. Transfer the tomatoes to the bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person chopping tomatoes and peppers on a cutting board." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Turkish-salsa.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82992-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Chop the seeded peppers finely and add them to the bowl.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82992-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Stir in the red pepper paste, lemon juice, parsley, sumac, and chili flakes (if using). Mix well to combine.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person mixing ezme salad ingredients in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Spicy-Turkish-ezme.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82992-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">If using, drizzle with pomegranate molasses and serve*.</div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-82992-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes about 2 to 2 1/2 cups of ezme, which is ideal for serving 4 people.&nbsp;The nutritional values below are per serving.</li>
<li><b>Storage: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Leftovers will keep well for 2-3 days when stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator.</span></li>
<li><b>*Let it rest before serving:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> It is optional, but if you have the time, chill it in the fridge for about 30 minutes before serving. This gives the ingredients a chance to mingle and develop deeper flavor. Just keep in mind that it will release some of its juices as it sits, so you may want to spoon out the excess liquid before bringing it to the table.</span></li>
<li><strong>Adjusting the spiciness:&nbsp;</strong>If you prefer your ezme to be on the milder side, I recommend taking the time to remove all of the seeds of your peppers and avoid using red pepper flakes.</li>
</ul></div></div>
